cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use drengr-hands in research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "drengr-hands: eyes and hands for AI agents on Android and iOS"
authors:
  - family-names: Sirajudeen
    given-names: Sharmin
    email: sharminsirajudeen11@gmail.com
version: 0.11.1
date-released: 2026-10-10
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/SharminSirajudeen/drengr-hands
url: https://drengr.dev
abstract: >-
  A vision-first actuation layer for mobile GUI agents. One Rust binary
  observes Android emulators, iOS simulators and cloud devices from
  screenshots and an optional accessibility tree, reports what changed after
  every action, and exposes the loop as an MCP server. On iOS it embeds a
  headless XCUITest runner in place of WebDriverAgent.
keywords:
  - GUI agents
  - mobile testing
  - Android
  - iOS
  - Model Context Protocol
